# Build context for the server image.
#
# The Dockerfile copies `package.json` and `src/` by name, so nothing here would
# reach the image. This file is about what reaches the *daemon*: every byte
# listed below is otherwise packed and uploaded before the first instruction
# runs, and with a remote build driver that copy leaves the machine.
#
# `.env*` is the one that matters. Those files hold the admin bearer and the
# grant-adjacent settings, and `.gitignore` already keeps them out of the repo —
# this keeps them out of the build context too, so a stray `docker build` in a
# checkout cannot ship them to a builder.

node_modules/
test/
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
*.tgz
*.log
.DS_Store
